// codebox_spec.gen -- f_wc stage 3: the spectral step. TWO real per-bin Gaussian kernel
// gains, ONE pass for both fields: KE = exp(-sig_e^2 k^2 / 2) multiplies the E pair (R,G),
// KI = exp(-sig_i^2 k^2 / 2) the I pair (B,A). 256x256 float32.
// Mirror: tests/modules/wc/wc_mirror.spec_stage().
//
// Input in1 = spectral texture (R,G = Re,Im of E-hat; B,A = Re,Im of I-hat).
//   - sigma is in PIXELS: the domain IS texels, so k = 2*pi*signed_bin/N (L = N; angular
//     units are load-bearing -- a cycles-unit k2 under-smooths the kernels by (2*pi)^2)
//   - sig_e = texture / sig_ratio (G6: the Psychedelic 2/2.9 aspect ratio 1.45 becomes
//     a dial, `aspect` -> Param sig_ratio; the 1.45 default is bit-neutral)
//   - NO decay multiplier and NO k = 0 (DC) zeroing -- both are KS-specific; the
//     dt-relaxation in the nl stage carries the decay (FR-002, settled model)
//   - there is no dt in this stage at all: dt only relaxes in nl (FR-003)
//   - signed bin index from floor(norm * N), not `cell` (bench-verified 2026-09-22)
//   - sig_i IS the user-facing `texture` dial, renamed here to avoid colliding with the
//     GLSL `texture()` builtin (unverified at codegen time); the definition maps
//     `texture` -> this Param (T025)
Param sig_i(1.4);
Param sig_ratio(1.45);

N = 256;
bx = floor(norm.x * N);
by = floor(norm.y * N);
mx = switch(bx < N * 0.5, bx, bx - N);
my = switch(by < N * 0.5, by, by - N);
kx = twopi / N * mx;
ky = twopi / N * my;
k2 = kx * kx + ky * ky;
se = sig_i / sig_ratio;
ge = exp(0 - 0.5 * se * se * k2);
gi = exp(0 - 0.5 * sig_i * sig_i * k2);

out1 = vec(nearest(in1, norm).x * ge, nearest(in1, norm).y * ge,
           nearest(in1, norm).z * gi, nearest(in1, norm).w * gi);
